      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.27,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Now, when you start writing tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 7.24,
          "en": "there are two super important questions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.24,
          "end": 10.07,
          "en": "you have to answer, relatively early.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.07,
          "end": 11.96,
          "en": "And, these questions are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.96,
          "end": 13.58,
          "en": "what you should test,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.58,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "and how you should test that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "And, I don't mean how you should technically test that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 22.62,
          "en": "So, how you make sure that you have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.62,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "that is then executed by some other tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "I'll come back to that technical question later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 29.93,
          "en": "but I mean, which kind of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.93,
          "end": 32.533,
          "en": "should you put into your testing code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.42,
          "end": 36.15,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to what to test,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 38.49,
          "en": "then, as mentioned for unit tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.49,
          "end": 40.69,
          "en": "you wanna test the different building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.69,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "that make up your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 44.16,
          "en": "and you really wanna test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.16,
          "end": 46.19,
          "en": "small building blocks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.19,
          "end": 49.35,
          "en": "so that you have small, focused tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.35,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "that only test one main thing each.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 56.32,
          "en": "So, that you really have a lot of focused tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.32,
          "end": 59.4,
          "en": "which then also fail for a clear reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 60.64,
          "en": "if they do fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.64,
          "end": 63.27,
          "en": "instead of having a few large tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.27,
          "end": 65.943,
          "en": "which could fail for all kinds of reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now regarding the \"how\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 72.05,
          "en": "you wanna test success and error cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.05,
          "end": 73.32,
          "en": "that could occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.32,
          "end": 76.58,
          "en": "if a user interacts with your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.58,
          "end": 78.02,
          "en": "And, you also, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.02,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "wanna test some rare,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "but possible scenarios and results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.4,
          "en": "And again, that will become a bit clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
